{"id": "EUVD-2026-59560", "enisaUuid": "bb6cf5b3-3e13-3bb1-be35-81f2c0a9a586", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw89: fix wrong pci_get_drvdata type in AER handlers\n\nrtw89 stores an ieee80211_hw pointer via pci_set_drvdata() at probe\ntime, but io_error_detected() and io_resume() retrieve it as a\nnet_device pointer.  This causes netif_device_detach/attach to\noperate on an ieee80211_hw struct, reading and writing at wrong\noffsets.  The adjacent io_slot_reset() already does it correctly.\n\nUse ieee80211_stop_queues/wake_queues instead, consistent with\nevery other queue stop/start path in the driver.\n\nTested on RTL8852CE by calling the handlers from a test module\nbefore and after the fix.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:44", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aefc30e4a829c1683f6ae999df7f9310c27eae6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1907b9a4fa9cb33d11a9af138374dd2e93f7a93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7068c379cf9aa8afe4dce4d9d82390187aa9c4d0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cq4j-9r28-wxqg", "CVE-2026-74413"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1191aef6-75f9-324a-b6ec-d76d370faec0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "16e3d93c6183649a3b210f82b83c1cb12aa5e8a3 <aefc30e4a829c1683f6ae999df7f9310c27eae6c"}, {"id": "59382d7b-af43-3d8f-ba26-cb30bf472456", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "93119aab-ddfc-302c-b476-62b3aa47401d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "16e3d93c6183649a3b210f82b83c1cb12aa5e8a3 <c1907b9a4fa9cb33d11a9af138374dd2e93f7a93"}, {"id": "9871b168-e813-3870-af0c-be98543f435f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "pa